Apple's research and development (R&D) spending increased by &#36;11.22 billion in fiscal 2026, reaching &#36;45.77 billion, according to the company's <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/pdfs/fy2026q4/FY26_Q4_Consolidated_Financial_Statements.pdf">financial statements</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2022/05/apple-park-sunset.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-844498" /><br/>
The figures represent a 32% increase from &#36;34.55 billion in fiscal 2025. That works out to roughly &#36;125 million a day spent on developing Apple's products and technologies during its financial year, which ended on September 26.<br/>
<br/>
Research spending grew considerably faster than sales. Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/02/apple-4q-2026-earnings/">annual revenue</a> increased 15%, while its R&D expenses rose by nearly a third. The company now spends close to one dollar on research and development for every ten dollars it brings in.<br/>
<br/>
Despite the annual jump, spending barely changed between the final two quarters of the year. Apple recorded &#36;11.730 billion in R&D expenses in the September quarter, just &#36;1 million more than the &#36;11.729 billion reported in its <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/pdfs/fy2026q3/FY26_Q3_Consolidated_Financial_Statements.pdf">June-quarter results</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Apple previously linked its growing development budget to AI. During its <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/30/apple-q2-2026-earnings-call/">April earnings call</a>, CFO Kevan Parekh said AI investment would come on top of spending already planned for Apple's product roadmap. Then-CEO <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/tim-cook/">Tim Cook</a> also highlighted increased R&D spending when asked about the company's AI investments.<br/>
